WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.262
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:14.532 --> 00:15.574
In the early years,

3
00:15.575 --> 00:17.576
there were not enough people in Hawaii

4
00:17.577 --> 00:19.620
to plant and harvest the fields,

5
00:19.621 --> 00:21.080
and to run the mills.

6
00:21.081 --> 00:22.957
So thousands of others came.

7
00:22.958 --> 00:24.167
Chinese.

8
00:24.501 --> 00:25.501
Portuguese.

9
00:25.794 --> 00:26.794
Japanese.

10
00:27.003 --> 00:28.004
Filipinos.

11
00:28.797 --> 00:31.924
People of many cultures, races, traditions,

12
00:31.925 --> 00:34.051
brought here by higher wages,

13
00:34.052 --> 00:35.845
by better living standards...

14
00:36.596 --> 00:40.809
sometimes by a freedom they could not find in their homeland.

15
01:35.113 --> 01:38.073
- No, do it this way. - Okay, I'll collect the money now.

16
01:38.074 --> 01:39.909
Dad, I'm going.

17
01:42.412 --> 01:43.663
Jorge.

18
01:45.248 --> 01:47.667
- Are you resigning today? - Dad...

19
01:48.543 --> 01:50.170
Nevermind.

20
01:51.212 --> 01:52.839
That miki looks delicious, Jorge.

21
01:53.923 --> 01:55.008
Yeah.

22
01:56.760 --> 01:57.886
You look busy.

23
01:58.303 --> 02:00.764
Your dad's making us do a lot of things. It's collection time.

24
02:01.890 --> 02:02.932
Alright.

25
02:03.975 --> 02:05.267
Jorge!

26
02:05.268 --> 02:06.727
Give some miki to your grandpa!

27
02:06.728 --> 02:08.021
I have it here.

28
02:11.816 --> 02:12.983
Okay, go.

29
02:12.984 --> 02:13.984
Yes.

30
02:14.402 --> 02:16.237
- Make it quick. - I'm on it.

31
02:18.990 --> 02:21.910
- Good morning, Auntie! - I saw your grandpa.

32
02:22.619 --> 02:24.412
He got there earlier than you.

33
02:25.121 --> 02:26.747
You're still here.

34
02:26.748 --> 02:29.375
You still jog even when it rains, Auntie?

35
02:29.376 --> 02:30.919
The rain stopped already.

36
02:31.378 --> 02:33.003
You know...

37
02:33.004 --> 02:36.257
If you really want to inherit the restaurant

38
02:38.676 --> 02:41.428
you must get there before your grandpa.

39
02:41.429 --> 02:43.555
That's my plan, Auntie.

40
02:43.556 --> 02:48.311
I'm telling you, your dad will come to his senses soon.

41
02:49.104 --> 02:51.730
- Take care, okay? - Yes, Auntie.

42
02:51.731 --> 02:52.731
Take care.

43
03:01.000 --> 03:07.000
"All the Things I Leave You" (Episode 1)

44
03:09.040 --> 03:10.083
Ruth!

45
03:10.542 --> 03:11.835
Ugly Ruth!

46
03:12.127 --> 03:14.128
Ruth, you flirt!

47
03:14.129 --> 03:15.797
- Come out now. - What?

48
03:16.756 --> 03:18.048
What?

49
03:18.049 --> 03:20.468
My god!

50
03:20.802 --> 03:23.303
- Don't rush me. - Wow!

51
03:23.304 --> 03:24.264
What?

52
03:24.265 --> 03:25.807
Enough with the makeup.

53
03:26.182 --> 03:28.851
You'll always be single anyway.

54
03:28.852 --> 03:29.852
Oh.

55
03:29.853 --> 03:32.187
Go ahead...

56
03:32.188 --> 03:34.606
Tell all the neighbors!

57
03:34.607 --> 03:37.110
- Just hurry up. - Wait, I'm coming.

58
03:41.906 --> 03:44.324
You're so slow.

59
03:44.325 --> 03:45.659
I said wait.

60
03:45.660 --> 03:47.078
Wait!

61
03:50.498 --> 03:52.791
I'm here now.

62
03:52.792 --> 03:55.210
Stop it, you'll spill the miki.

63
03:55.211 --> 03:57.004
You should've brought some for me!

64
03:57.005 --> 03:59.549
You already ate so much while I was cooking.

65
04:00.800 --> 04:02.677
I didn't think there'd be any left.

66
04:03.470 --> 04:05.012
You're so mean.

67
04:05.013 --> 04:07.306
Do I look like a pig to you?

68
04:07.307 --> 04:09.683
Ugh, keep up.

69
04:09.684 --> 04:11.226
Yes, boss.

70
04:11.227 --> 04:12.770
Right behind you.

71
04:13.062 --> 04:15.898
You're so slow.

72
04:15.899 --> 04:17.441
There are no more tricycles around

73
04:17.442 --> 04:19.651
and a lot of people are waiting.

74
04:19.652 --> 04:22.821
So what, it's my fault?

75
04:22.822 --> 04:24.616
Yes, it's your fault.

76
04:25.200 --> 04:26.576
And why is that?

77
04:26.826 --> 04:28.494
You're too slow.

78
04:28.495 --> 04:30.579
Keep an eye out for passing tricycles.

79
04:30.580 --> 04:31.873
Sure.

80
04:41.841 --> 04:42.841
Hey.

81
04:43.843 --> 04:45.677
Don't walk near the puddle.

82
04:45.678 --> 04:47.346
Do you want to get splashed with water?

83
04:47.347 --> 04:48.347
Oh,

84
04:48.431 --> 04:49.765
My bad.

85
04:49.766 --> 04:51.683
I didn't notice.

86
04:51.684 --> 04:55.521
Cutie said good morning to me.

87
04:55.522 --> 04:58.398
Who's Cutie? Cutie can wait.

88
04:58.399 --> 05:01.611
You wait. I'm still thinking of a reply.

89
05:04.155 --> 05:05.782
Who was that?!

90
05:06.115 --> 05:07.157
That guy's a jerk.

91
05:07.158 --> 05:09.452
Should we run after him?

92
05:11.037 --> 05:12.913
I hope you fall from your motorcycle!

93
05:12.914 --> 05:14.749
Idiot, we'll have you arrested!

94
05:15.458 --> 05:16.876
Look at your shirt.

95
05:17.710 --> 05:19.962
Let's go home and change.

96
05:19.963 --> 05:21.255
Did you get his plate number?

97
05:21.256 --> 05:22.256
No, I didn't.

98
05:23.299 --> 05:26.009
But I'll recognize him when I see him again.

99
05:26.010 --> 05:27.928
And then I'll punch him in the face.

100
05:27.929 --> 05:29.222
You're a mess.

101
05:31.099 --> 05:32.642
I'll just change at the restaurant.

102
05:33.101 --> 05:34.018
Look, there's a tricycle now.

103
05:34.018 --> 05:35.018
Hey!

104
06:29.741 --> 06:32.368
Good morning, Grandpa Tino.

105
06:33.786 --> 06:35.455
Why are you late?

106
06:36.164 --> 06:37.789
I'm sorry, Grandpa.

107
06:37.790 --> 06:39.416
There weren't any tricycles around.

108
06:39.417 --> 06:44.504
There was a rude rider that splashed mud on my shirt.

109
06:44.505 --> 06:48.258
I was thinking about what you said.

110
06:48.259 --> 06:50.928
The delivery app for the restaurant.

111
06:51.596 --> 06:54.098
Yes, Grandpa. Trust me.

112
06:54.641 --> 06:57.184
A lot of customers want deliveries.

113
06:57.185 --> 07:00.979
We need to be up to date with social media and...

114
07:00.980 --> 07:02.065
Enough.

115
07:02.940 --> 07:05.150
There's an applicant already.

116
07:05.151 --> 07:06.402
Really?

117
07:07.111 --> 07:08.111
Yes!

118
07:09.822 --> 07:11.156
You'll be the one to interview him

119
07:11.157 --> 07:14.242
because I don't know anything about social media.

120
07:14.243 --> 07:17.121
I have a doctor's appointment.

121
07:18.539 --> 07:20.457
But an applicant will come here later.

122
07:20.458 --> 07:21.458
I can do it, Grandpa.

123
07:21.459 --> 07:25.796
I'll tell him to manage our social media pages

124
07:25.797 --> 07:29.300
as well as do the deliveries.

125
07:29.634 --> 07:31.510
Yes, everything you said.

126
07:31.511 --> 07:33.845
Do this well.

127
07:33.846 --> 07:37.350
Show me you can manage the restaurant.

128
07:38.059 --> 07:39.185
Thank you, Grandpa.

129
07:45.983 --> 07:47.067
Jorge!

130
07:47.068 --> 07:49.653
Wait, I'm changing my shirt.

131
07:49.654 --> 07:51.989
Do it faster and come here.

132
07:54.242 --> 07:55.409
What?

133
07:55.410 --> 07:57.078
Did someone tell you already?

134
07:57.745 --> 08:00.664
That you look like Grandpa Tino when he was young?

135
08:00.665 --> 08:02.457
Everyone says that.

136
08:02.458 --> 08:04.502
I told you, that's really me.

137
08:05.586 --> 08:07.254
That's why

138
08:07.255 --> 08:09.465
this restaurant is my destiny.

139
08:09.966 --> 08:12.802
Wow, that makes so much sense.

140
08:13.386 --> 08:15.263
You're both grumpy old men.

141
08:18.099 --> 08:18.975
Ruth.

142
08:18.976 --> 08:20.226
What?

143
08:21.121 --> 08:25.040
Has anybody told you that you look like dinakdakan [choppped pork]?

144
08:25.064 --> 08:26.983
Damn you.

145
08:27.358 --> 08:29.276
Well, at least it's delicious.

146
08:29.277 --> 08:32.739
Oh, spoiled dinakdakan.

147
08:38.202 --> 08:40.704
Jorge, isn't that...

148
08:40.705 --> 08:42.915
You're right, it's him.

149
08:53.801 --> 08:56.261
Hey, he actually looks nice.

150
08:56.262 --> 08:58.805
Ruth, don't forget what he did.

151
08:58.806 --> 09:00.182
I can let go.

152
09:00.183 --> 09:02.893
Look, he's kind of cute.

153
09:02.894 --> 09:04.479
Stop that.

154
09:04.604 --> 09:06.354
Go wash in the kitchen.

155
09:06.355 --> 09:08.441
You're no fun.

156
09:11.986 --> 09:14.822
Sir, I'm here for a job.

157
09:19.786 --> 09:21.536
My name is Kiko Cablayan.

158
09:21.537 --> 09:24.164
I'm applying for the position of social media manager

159
09:24.165 --> 09:25.666
and delivery boy.

160
09:38.721 --> 09:40.389
You don't recognize me?

161
09:43.100 --> 09:45.852
Were we classmates in grade school?

162
09:45.853 --> 09:46.853
No.

163
09:47.522 --> 09:50.565
You splashed mud on me on the way here.

164
09:50.566 --> 09:55.321
Oh, you're the ones waiting in the middle of the road.

165
09:57.615 --> 09:59.075
I didn't mean to.

166
10:00.868 --> 10:03.412
Is the owner here?

167
10:05.331 --> 10:10.837
We don't accept crazy people here.

168
10:12.004 --> 10:13.214
How come?

169
10:13.881 --> 10:15.882
Are you the owner?

170
10:15.883 --> 10:16.968
No.

171
10:18.177 --> 10:19.678
Not yet.

172
10:19.679 --> 10:21.139
So, you're not.

173
10:21.889 --> 10:23.349
You're all talk.

174
10:23.850 --> 10:27.061
Did I do anything wrong, huh?

175
10:28.104 --> 10:29.355
You're fired.

176
10:30.189 --> 10:32.149
But I'm not hired yet.

177
10:36.070 --> 10:37.113
Okay, fine.

178
10:39.448 --> 10:40.491
You're hired.

179
10:42.243 --> 10:43.369
You're fired!

180
10:43.911 --> 10:44.996
Get out.

181
10:45.413 --> 10:47.330
You're hired and then you're fired.

182
10:47.331 --> 10:50.585
You're not even the owner.

183
10:51.210 --> 10:53.628
What's going on here?

184
10:53.629 --> 10:54.672
Bong?

185
10:59.802 --> 11:03.763
Good morning, sir. I'm Kiko Cablayan.

186
11:03.764 --> 11:05.641
Are you the applicant?

187
11:06.100 --> 11:08.310
Yes, sir. Kiko.

188
11:08.311 --> 11:09.645
Where are you from?

189
11:09.979 --> 11:13.733
I'm from Cagayan but now I live in Ilocos.

190
11:14.483 --> 11:15.192
That's good.

191
11:15.193 --> 11:17.445
You can start right away.

192
11:18.529 --> 11:22.198
- We have a lot of deliveries. - But Grandpa...

193
11:22.199 --> 11:26.244
And Kiko, I believe you will do your best for this job.

194
11:26.245 --> 11:28.289
For sure, boss!

195
11:32.752 --> 11:34.629
Grandpa...

196
11:36.130 --> 11:37.673
- Grandpa, wait. - What now?

197
11:38.633 --> 11:41.010
I bet this will fit you perfectly.

198
11:42.678 --> 11:43.803
Yes, sir.

199
11:43.804 --> 11:45.681
This is perfect.

200
11:47.767 --> 11:49.100
Kiko...

201
11:49.101 --> 11:55.649
Jorge will brief you about your tasks.

202
11:55.650 --> 11:56.650
Yes, sir.

203
11:57.234 --> 12:00.863
But he didn't pass...

204
12:01.781 --> 12:03.658
Grandpa!

205
12:09.664 --> 12:11.998
You already know how to manage a social media page, right?

206
12:11.999 --> 12:13.960
I don't need to teach you?

207
12:14.460 --> 12:16.378
Have you seen my social media profile?

208
12:16.379 --> 12:17.462
I saw it.

209
12:17.463 --> 12:18.965
Are you stalking me?

210
12:19.423 --> 12:20.548
Background check.

211
12:20.549 --> 12:22.718
That's what you call background check.

212
12:28.766 --> 12:31.142
Are you being the boss again?

213
12:31.143 --> 12:32.143
Yes.

214
12:34.772 --> 12:36.440
No.

215
12:38.651 --> 12:40.443
- Are you or are you not? - I am.

216
12:40.444 --> 12:44.030
As long as Grandpa Tino isn't here, I'm the boss.

217
12:44.031 --> 12:46.658
If he's here, he's the boss.

218
12:46.659 --> 12:49.036
But Boss Tino is here.

219
12:49.495 --> 12:50.495
He's not.

220
12:50.913 --> 12:52.289
He left.

221
12:54.208 --> 12:56.002
Okay, boss.

222
12:56.419 --> 12:57.837
Don't call me boss.

223
12:58.212 --> 12:59.505
You're making me look old.

224
13:00.339 --> 13:02.216
Then what? Jorge?

225
13:03.676 --> 13:05.386
How do you know my name?

226
13:05.928 --> 13:07.263
I heard it earlier.

227
13:08.222 --> 13:09.724
Are you stalking me?

228
13:11.600 --> 13:13.853
Background check.

229
13:16.230 --> 13:20.358
You'll do everything for the social media page.

230
13:20.359 --> 13:24.279
You'll answer the queries

231
13:24.280 --> 13:27.908
and you'll also deliver.

232
13:28.826 --> 13:30.618
Understood?

233
13:30.619 --> 13:32.079
Yes, Jorge.

234
13:32.455 --> 13:34.248
Are we friends now?

235
13:36.375 --> 13:37.543
No.

236
13:39.378 --> 13:40.796
Jorge!

237
15:12.858 --> 15:14.609
Come to work early tomorrow, okay?

238
15:14.640 --> 15:16.183
Get home safe.

239
15:16.767 --> 15:17.767
Jorge!

240
15:17.845 --> 15:19.304
I'll drive you home.

241
15:20.104 --> 15:21.729
Right on time! My feet hurt already.

242
15:21.730 --> 15:23.399
Wait, I'll get my helmet.

243
15:23.774 --> 15:24.774
Ruth...

244
15:24.859 --> 15:26.110
Jorge, come on.

245
15:28.404 --> 15:29.571
Come on.

246
15:29.572 --> 15:30.447
I don't want to.

247
15:30.448 --> 15:32.198
You're being stubborn again.

248
15:32.199 --> 15:33.408
You can't make me.

249
15:33.409 --> 15:34.409
Come on!

250
15:35.286 --> 15:36.287
Come on!

251
15:37.454 --> 15:41.125
Stop it, Ruth. I said no.

252
15:49.049 --> 15:52.052
- Stop it, Ruth. - It's so fun!

253
15:54.263 --> 15:56.181
You should've made me sit in the middle.

254
15:56.182 --> 15:57.515
Why?

255
15:57.516 --> 15:59.058
So, I could eat your hair?

256
15:59.059 --> 16:01.812
You're such a crybaby. That's why there's a helmet.

257
16:03.355 --> 16:06.149
It's a good thing your cousin's helmet fit Jorge's head.

258
16:06.150 --> 16:07.901
Focus on the road!

259
16:07.902 --> 16:10.195
Look at Jorge's head, it's so big.

260
16:10.196 --> 16:11.113
Right?

261
16:11.114 --> 16:12.448
Oh really?

262
16:13.157 --> 16:14.407
I swear if it gets bumpy,

263
16:14.408 --> 16:17.619
watch out, I'll push you.

264
16:17.620 --> 16:19.787
Hold me tightly...

265
16:19.788 --> 16:22.499
...so you won't fall.

266
16:24.460 --> 16:26.128
Ruth, stop it!

267
16:26.670 --> 16:28.087
Go faster.

268
16:28.088 --> 16:30.256
I want to go home already.

269
16:30.257 --> 16:31.257
Why?

270
16:31.258 --> 16:32.801
Are we friends now?

271
16:34.803 --> 16:37.305
You're just giving us a ride,

272
16:37.306 --> 16:38.973
what do you mean we're friends now?

273
16:38.974 --> 16:40.642
You're not that lucky.

274
16:40.643 --> 16:42.937
Just asking.

275
16:45.940 --> 16:48.524
Ruth, are you having fun?

276
16:48.525 --> 16:51.320
Yes! Go faster!

277
17:06.085 --> 17:08.044
What's going on, Auntie?

278
17:08.045 --> 17:10.463
Jorge, your grandpa.

279
17:10.464 --> 17:11.547
What happened?

280
17:11.548 --> 17:13.258
The ambulance just left.

281
17:13.259 --> 17:16.220
Your father said to meet them at the hospital.

282
17:17.221 --> 17:18.055
But how?

283
17:18.056 --> 17:22.685
Ask your friend to give you a ride to Laoag.

284
17:24.103 --> 17:26.105
Auntie, what do you mean?

285
17:27.982 --> 17:29.984
Just ask your friend.

286
17:30.234 --> 17:32.236
Auntie...

287
17:32.736 --> 17:35.239
He was still okay at the restaurant.

288
17:36.198 --> 17:37.740
Why? How?

289
17:37.741 --> 17:39.326
Why would he be rushed to the hospital?

290
17:39.660 --> 17:41.953
What did he do yesterday?

291
17:41.954 --> 17:44.248
I don't know. He was in bed the whole afternoon.

292
17:44.665 --> 17:45.791
What did he eat?

293
17:46.250 --> 17:48.501
He ate rice. He was still strong yesterday.

294
17:48.502 --> 17:50.754
And he was still strong earlier.

295
17:52.214 --> 17:55.592
I don't know about grandpa. I don't know.

296
18:12.192 --> 18:13.276
Ruth.

297
18:13.277 --> 18:14.694
Stay here.

298
18:14.695 --> 18:15.778
Take care, okay?

299
18:15.779 --> 18:16.905
I will.

300
18:31.295 --> 18:35.466
- Ruth, take charge here. - Yes.

301
18:46.185 --> 18:47.852
Dear Bong,

302
18:47.853 --> 18:52.732
I always think of what will happen.

303
18:52.733 --> 19:00.239
Will things fall into place or will we always be like this?

304
19:00.240 --> 19:02.867
always unsure

305
19:02.868 --> 19:07.331
always dreading if this is all that the world has for us...

306
19:41.323 --> 19:43.325
Bong.

307
19:44.743 --> 19:47.996
Are we going to Hawaii?

308
19:57.423 --> 20:00.508
How about you, Bong?

309
20:00.509 --> 20:04.804
Do you also ask yourself what will happen to us in the future?

310
20:04.805 --> 20:08.724
Who are we going to be?

311
20:08.725 --> 20:10.476
Where are we going to be?

312
20:10.477 --> 20:13.354
What do our future selves look like?

313
20:13.355 --> 20:15.606
Will things get better?

314
20:15.607 --> 20:17.900
Will our problems end?

315
20:17.901 --> 20:22.364
Will the world become a better place for us?

316
20:34.251 --> 20:36.462
Kiko...

317
20:41.341 --> 20:43.343
Thank you.

318
20:49.641 --> 20:52.186
We're friends now.

319
20:59.151 --> 21:00.778
Jorge, my helmet...
